{
  "manufacturer": "Circutor",
  "model": "CVM-C5",
  "short_model": "CVM-C5",
  "aliases": [
    "CVM-C5-ITF-485",
    "CVM-C5-MC-485",
    "CVM-C5-mV-485"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter",
  "applies_to": "Circutor CVM-C5 panel power analyzer, RS-485 Modbus RTU versions (ITF-485, MC-485, mV-485), manual M026B01-03.",
  "summary": "The CVM-C5 is a compact panel power analyzer from Circutor with an RS-485 Modbus RTU port. Every measured value is a 32-bit integer in two registers with fixed scaling (V x10, mA, Hz x10, % x10), read with function 03 or 04, each with instantaneous, maximum and minimum copies. This map covers voltages, currents, reactive and apparent power, frequency, THD, demand and the two-tariff energy counters plus the tariff selector.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "All Modbus addresses in the manual are hexadecimal wire addresses. The manual's example reads L1-L2 voltage at initial register 2A and receives 0000 084D = 212.5 V, which matches the table entry 2A-2B with V x10 scaling."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "CVM-C5 Instruction Manual",
    "doc_number": "M026B01-03",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://docs.circutor.com/docs/M026B01-03.pdf",
    "pages": "Section 4.7, PDF pp. 43-46 (tables 17-18)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Word order: the manual's example response gives register 1 = 0000 and register 2 = 084D for 212.5 V, so 32-bit values are high word first (ABCD). The manual states all parameters are 32 bits long.",
    "Left out: active power, signed reactive power, power factor and cos phi (per phase and three-phase), because the manual does not state whether those Modbus values are signed.",
    "Left out: the 'Maximum demand' register at 44-45, whose unit is printed as W/VA/mA, so its unit depends on the selected demand variable.",
    "Left out: apparent energy (consumed and generated) because the units column prints kVAh for one and VAh for the other; CO2, cost and hours per tariff.",
    "Energy counters are per tariff only (T1 and T2); there is no total register.",
    "Frequency is scaled x10 on this model (not x100 as on the CVM-C10)."
  ],
